; ================================================================================================
; MOVEMENT SPEC of the SpaceZipper algebra (v2 — the certified core).
;
; DESIGN.  A zipper is (context, focus).  Two SORTS keep the distinction the previous model erased:
;   Z — SPACES (path sets) and the space operators, including space-level navigation `Sub k z`
;       (the subspace under item k).  `Unwrap` is a space op and equals `Sub` denotationally.
;   C — CURSORS: `(Root z)` and the MOVEMENTS `Descend k c` / `Ascend c`.  The movement monoid is
;       words over {Descend k, Ascend} acting (partially) on C with the relation
;           Ascend (Descend k c) = c                       [the zipper contract; Ascend at Root is
;                                                           deliberately undefined/stuck]
;       `FocusOf : C -> Z` interprets a cursor, and the commuting law
;           FocusOf (Descend k c) = Sub k (FocusOf c)
;       separates movement (C) from space navigation (Z): they agree on focus, but only Descend is
;       invertible by Ascend — Unwrap/Sub build a NEW root.  (Sort separation makes it impossible
;       for an e-class to confuse them.)
;
; LOCK-STEP INVARIANT.  A cursor over a virtual space is ONE focus into the composite; every `Sub`
; rule pushes THE SAME key k into every Z-operand of an operator (this is what makes Ascend commute
; with every operator and the whole design work).  The invariant is a syntactic property of the
; rules below and is enforced mechanically by scripts/lint_zipper_egg.py.
;
; OBSERVATIONS (the full set — see the ops x observations matrix in zipper-egg-tests/README.md):
;   Term z      : is the focus path a member?                                   B
;   Sub k z     : the subspace one item down (space-level navigation)            Z
;   Keys z      : the EXACT present child keys at the focus                      KL
;                 local for ∅/ε/∪/Guard and concrete sources; for Wrap1 it needs one child
;                 IsEmpty; for ∩ \ · <| it is a bounded child-emptiness SEARCH (each candidate key
;                 is kept iff its subspace is non-empty) — the honest cost, stated per-op below.
;                 NOTE (learned the hard way): in an e-graph Keys CANNOT be an over-approximation —
;                 every equated observation must be a FUNCTION of the denotation, or congruence
;                 equates two different approximations of one e-class (e.g. Keys{∅} via the ∅ node
;                 vs via the Wrap1-of-∅ node) and poisons the graph.  Exactness is soundness here.
;   IsEmpty z   : is the whole subspace empty?  ⟺ ¬Term z ∧ Keys z = [] — decided locally for
;                 ∅/ε/Wrap1/∪, a search (via Keys) for ∩ \ · <|, stated as such.
;   over an OPAQUE trie node (Src n) the observations are the named uninterpreted symbols
;   (TermOf n) (EmptyOf n) (KeysOf n) and `Sub k (Src n) = Src (ChildOf n k)` — an O(1) child
;   lookup.  Movements over opaque sources reduce to NORMAL FORMS in these symbols (never dead-end,
;   never touch the subtree) — that is the locality claim, and it now holds for EVERY operator.
;
; KEY ENUMERATION IS THE HARD PART of a virtual zipper, so it is a first-class observation with a
; merge algebra (KMerge/KInter/KGuard) and per-candidate emptiness filtering (KFilt), and
; TailsUnion/TailsIntersection/Head/Iter are DEFINED through it — exact keys everywhere (a spurious
; ∅ would poison a meet / a body; and see the e-graph exactness note above).
;
; ITER is the head-DEPENDENT iteration: bodies are defunctionalized as the `Body` sort with
;   App b h t  — apply body b to head h and tail-space t
; so any program can add a body constructor + one App rule (JoinBody = the datalog join; InvBody =
; relation inversion, demonstrating head capture; ConstBody = the invariant-body Iter, ported from
; formal.egg together with the IterUnion hoisting soundness counterexamples).
;
; COST CONTRACT (checked, not asserted: see zipper-egg-tests/locality-schedule.egg and the linter):
;   * one movement/observation step rewrites ONLY the top constructor — cost O(size of the op
;     expression at the focus), with ZERO dependence on trie size or subtree contents;
;   * a chain of d descents is d such steps (mechanized by per-layer saturation in the schedule
;     file: the checks pass after exactly d+c micro-phases and provably not before);
;   * state growth: O(1) frames per move per Composition/Restriction node (each descent through ·
;     adds one Guard/Union frame) — "local in the op expression", NOT constant-size;
;   * no observation rule constructs concrete trie nodes (linted: no Node/CC on any obs RHS).
;   * IsEmpty on ∩ \ · <| and KeysX are searches (documented above), used only where exactness is
;     semantically required.
;
; Everything here is a claim ∀vars. LHS = RHS over the denotation; the universal proofs live in
; proofs/*.smt2 (z3) and proofs/*.p-style obligations (vampire --induction) — egglog runs the
; algebra, the provers certify the rules.  This file's checks are ground REGRESSIONS (including
; every previously-stuck probe), not the proofs.
; ================================================================================================

; ---- abstract concrete-trie node: a base node or an O(1) child lookup ----
(datatype Node (N i64) (ChildOf Node i64))

(datatype*
  (B (T) (F)
     (Not B) (Or B B) (And B B) (AndNot B B)   ; AndNot a b = a ∧ ¬b
     (Eqi i64 i64)                             ; decidable item equality
     (TermOf Node)                             ; uninterpreted: is the opaque node terminal?
     (EmptyOf Node)                            ; uninterpreted: is the opaque node empty?
     (Term Z)                                  ; membership at the focus
     (IsEmpty Z)                               ; emptiness of the whole subspace (search for ∩ \ · <|)
     (IsNilK KL)                               ; helper: is a key list empty?
     (TermAt C))                               ; membership at a CURSOR focus
  (KL (KNil) (KCons i64 KL)
      (KeysOf Node)                            ; uninterpreted: (exact) keys of an opaque node
      (Keys Z)                                 ; EXACT present keys (see header note)
      (KMerge KL KL) (KInter KL KL)            ; sorted merge / sorted intersect
      (KGuard B KL)                            ; KGuard T ks = ks ; KGuard F ks = KNil
      (KFilt KL Z) (KConsIf i64 B KL)          ; keep a candidate key iff its subspace is non-empty
      (KeysAt C))
  (Z (Empty)                                   ; ∅
     (Eps)                                     ; {ε}
     (Src Node)                                ; opaque concrete trie node
     (Wrap1 i64 Z)                             ; {k·p : p ∈ z}
     (Union Z Z) (Intersection Z Z) (Subtraction Z Z) (Composition Z Z)
     (Restriction Z Z)                         ; keep x-paths having a prefix in p (TOTAL semantics)
     (Restr Z Z)                               ; compat alias for the transpiler (= Restriction)
     (Raffination Z Z)                         ; x \| y = x \ (x <| y)
     (TailsUnion Z) (TailsIntersection Z) (Head Z)
     (Unwrap i64 Z)                            ; space op: subspace under k (= Sub; NOT a movement)
     (Iter Z Body)                             ; head-dependent iteration over present keys
     (Guard B Z)                               ; Guard T z = z ; Guard F z = ∅
     (Sub i64 Z)                               ; space-level navigation: the subspace under k
     (KFoldU KL Z) (KFoldI KL Z)               ; ∪ / ∩ of (Sub h z) over a key list
     (HFold KL)                                ; Head fold
     (IFold KL Z Body)                         ; Iter fold
     (App Body i64 Z)                          ; defunctionalized body application
     (FocusOf C))                              ; the space at a cursor's focus
  (Body (ConstBody Z)                          ; invariant body (formal.egg's Iter)
        (JoinBody Z)                           ; datalog join body: h,t ↦ h·⋃(s <| t)
        (InvBody) (InvBody2 i64)               ; relation inversion (head capture across levels)
        (BodyK i64 IL ZL))                     ; program-defined bodies: index + captured items/spaces
                                               ; (each program adds its own App rules for its BodyK ids)
  (IL (INil) (ICons i64 IL))                   ; captured item lists (outer iteration heads)
  (ZL (ZNil) (ZCons Z ZL))                     ; captured space lists (free operands of a body)
  (C (Root Z) (Descend i64 C) (Ascend C)))

; ================================================================================================
; booleans
; ================================================================================================
(rewrite (Not (T)) (F)) (rewrite (Not (F)) (T)) (rewrite (Not (Not b)) b)   ; definitional (boolean tables)
(rewrite (Or  (T) b) (T)) (rewrite (Or  b (T)) (T)) (rewrite (Or  (F) b) b) (rewrite (Or  b (F)) b)   ; definitional (boolean tables)
(rewrite (And (F) b) (F)) (rewrite (And b (F)) (F)) (rewrite (And (T) b) b) (rewrite (And b (T)) b)   ; definitional (boolean tables)
(rewrite (AndNot (F) b) (F)) (rewrite (AndNot (T) b) (Not b))          ; left rules (were missing)   ; definitional (boolean tables)
(rewrite (AndNot a (T)) (F)) (rewrite (AndNot a (F)) a)   ; definitional (boolean tables)
(rewrite (Eqi a a) (T))   ; definitional (boolean tables)
(rule ((= e (Eqi a b)) (!= a b)) ((union e (F))))   ; definitional (boolean tables)

; ---- conditional space ----
(rewrite (Guard (T) z) z)   ; definitional (conditional)
(rewrite (Guard (F) z) (Empty))   ; definitional (conditional)

; ================================================================================================
; MOVEMENT (cursors): the zipper contract and the focus interpretation
; ================================================================================================
(rewrite (Ascend (Descend k c)) c)             ; Ascend ∘ Descend k = id  (Ascend at Root: stuck)   ; definitional (the zipper contract; tested in SCOPE 1)
(rewrite (FocusOf (Root z)) z)   ; definitional (cursor interpretation)
(rewrite (FocusOf (Descend k c)) (Sub k (FocusOf c)))   ; movement agrees with space navigation   ; definitional (cursor interpretation)
(rewrite (TermAt c) (Term (FocusOf c)))   ; definitional (cursor interpretation)
(rewrite (KeysAt c) (Keys (FocusOf c)))   ; definitional (cursor interpretation)

; ================================================================================================
; Term — membership at the focus (total; one combinator per operator)
; ================================================================================================
(rewrite (Term (Empty)) (F))   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2, proofs/wrap1.smt2
(rewrite (Term (Eps)) (T))   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2, proofs/wrap1.smt2
(rewrite (Term (Src n)) (TermOf n))            ; opaque: the NAMED flag (composition etc. stay live)   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2, proofs/wrap1.smt2
(rewrite (Term (Wrap1 h z)) (F))   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2, proofs/wrap1.smt2
(rewrite (Term (Union a b)) (Or (Term a) (Term b)))   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2 + proofs/threeway_{union,intersection,subtraction}.smt2
(rewrite (Term (Intersection a b)) (And (Term a) (Term b)))   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2 + proofs/threeway_{union,intersection,subtraction}.smt2
(rewrite (Term (Subtraction a b)) (AndNot (Term a) (Term b)))   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2 + proofs/threeway_{union,intersection,subtraction}.smt2
(rewrite (Term (Composition a b)) (And (Term a) (Term b)))   ; proof: proofs/composition.smt2
(rewrite (Term (Restriction x p)) (And (Term x) (Term p)))   ; TOTAL — ε∈(x<|p) ⟺ ε∈x ∧ ε∈p   ; proof: proofs/restriction.smt2
(rewrite (Term (Guard b z)) (And b (Term z)))   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2, proofs/wrap1.smt2
(rewrite (Term (Head z)) (F))                  ; heads are length-1 paths, never ε   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2, proofs/wrap1.smt2
; Unwrap/Raffination/Restr/tails/Iter reduce structurally first (below), then Term applies.

; ================================================================================================
; Sub — space-level navigation (one LOCAL step per operator; same k into every operand = lock-step)
; ================================================================================================
(rewrite (Sub k (Empty)) (Empty))   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2 (locality: scripts/check_locality.sh)
(rewrite (Sub k (Eps)) (Empty))   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2 (locality: scripts/check_locality.sh)
(rewrite (Sub k (Src n)) (Src (ChildOf n k)))  ; O(1) child lookup — the subtree is NEVER traversed   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2 (locality: scripts/check_locality.sh)
(rewrite (Sub k (Wrap1 h z)) (Guard (Eqi k h) z))   ; proof: proofs/wrap1.smt2
(rewrite (Sub k (Union a b)) (Union (Sub k a) (Sub k b)))   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2
(rewrite (Sub k (Intersection a b)) (Intersection (Sub k a) (Sub k b)))   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2
(rewrite (Sub k (Subtraction a b)) (Subtraction (Sub k a) (Sub k b)))   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2
(rewrite (Sub k (Composition a b)) (Union (Composition (Sub k a) b) (Guard (Term a) (Sub k b))))   ; proof: proofs/composition.smt2
; TOTAL restriction step: a surviving prefix either ended at the focus (ε∈p ⇒ keep all of x's
; branch) or continues under k — no "p not terminal" invariant required, no unsound F.
(rewrite (Sub k (Restriction x p)) (Union (Guard (Term p) (Sub k x)) (Restriction (Sub k x) (Sub k p))))   ; proof: proofs/restriction.smt2
(rewrite (Sub k (Guard b z)) (Guard b (Sub k z)))   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2 (locality: scripts/check_locality.sh)

; ---- space ops that DEFINE themselves via other ops (macros / aliases) ----
(rewrite (Unwrap k z) (Sub k z))               ; unwrap is space navigation (a NEW root, not a move)   ; definitional (unwrap IS space navigation)
(rewrite (Restr x p) (Restriction x p))        ; transpiler-compat alias (Restriction now total)   ; definitional (alias)
(rewrite (Raffination x y) (Subtraction x (Restriction x y)))   ; definitional (macro; behaviour via restriction.smt2)
(rewrite (Restriction x (Eps)) x)              ; every path has ε as a prefix   ; proof: proofs/restriction.smt2
(rewrite (Restriction (Empty) p) (Empty))   ; proof: proofs/restriction.smt2
(rewrite (Restriction x (Empty)) (Empty))   ; proof: proofs/restriction.smt2
; sound e-class collapse when a prefix provably ends at the focus (the old smart constructor):
(rule ((= e (Restriction x p))) ((Term p)))   ; demand-materialisation (creates the guard term; asserts nothing)
(rule ((= e (Restriction x p)) (= (T) (Term p))) ((union e x)))   ; proof: proofs/restriction.smt2 (terminal-prefix collapse)

; ================================================================================================
; Keys — the EXACT child-key observation.  Local for ∅/ε/∪/Guard/Src; Wrap1 needs one child
; IsEmpty; ∩ \ · <| filter their CANDIDATE lists by per-key subspace emptiness (KFilt) — the
; documented bounded search.  Exactness is what keeps observations e-class-consistent.
; ================================================================================================
(rewrite (Keys (Empty)) (KNil))   ; definitional (exact by construction)
(rewrite (Keys (Eps)) (KNil))   ; definitional (exact by construction)
(rewrite (Keys (Src n)) (KeysOf n))            ; opaque: the NAMED (exact) key set   ; definitional (exact by construction)
(rewrite (Keys (Wrap1 h z)) (KConsIf h (IsEmpty z) (KNil)))   ; proof: proofs/keys_filter_exact.smt2 (presence ⟺ child nonempty)
(rewrite (Keys (Union a b)) (KMerge (Keys a) (Keys b)))   ; proof: proofs/refine_kmerge.smt2
(rewrite (Keys (Guard b z)) (KGuard b (Keys z)))   ; definitional (exact by construction)
(rewrite (Keys (Intersection a b))   ; proof: proofs/keys_intersection.smt2 + proofs/refine_kinter.smt2 + proofs/keys_filter_exact.smt2
         (KFilt (KInter (Keys a) (Keys b)) (Intersection a b)))
(rewrite (Keys (Subtraction a b))   ; proof: proofs/keys_subtraction.smt2 + proofs/keys_filter_exact.smt2
         (KFilt (Keys a) (Subtraction a b)))
(rewrite (Keys (Composition a b))   ; proof: proofs/keys_composition.smt2 + proofs/keys_filter_exact.smt2
         (KFilt (KMerge (Keys a) (KGuard (Term a) (Keys b))) (Composition a b)))
(rewrite (Keys (Restriction x p))   ; proof: proofs/keys_restriction.smt2 + proofs/keys_filter_exact.smt2
         (KFilt (KMerge (KGuard (Term p) (Keys x)) (KInter (Keys x) (Keys p))) (Restriction x p)))

; sorted merge / intersect (key-ascending lists, like the implementation's child lists)
(rewrite (KMerge (KNil) c) c) (rewrite (KMerge c (KNil)) c)   ; proof: proofs/refine_kmerge.smt2
(rule ((= e (KMerge (KCons k1 r1) (KCons k2 r2))) (< k1 k2)) ((union e (KCons k1 (KMerge r1 (KCons k2 r2))))))   ; proof: proofs/refine_kmerge.smt2
(rule ((= e (KMerge (KCons k1 r1) (KCons k2 r2))) (< k2 k1)) ((union e (KCons k2 (KMerge (KCons k1 r1) r2)))))   ; proof: proofs/refine_kmerge.smt2
(rule ((= e (KMerge (KCons k1 r1) (KCons k2 r2))) (= k1 k2)) ((union e (KCons k1 (KMerge r1 r2)))))   ; proof: proofs/refine_kmerge.smt2
(rewrite (KInter (KNil) c) (KNil)) (rewrite (KInter c (KNil)) (KNil))   ; proof: proofs/refine_kinter.smt2
(rule ((= e (KInter (KCons k1 r1) (KCons k2 r2))) (< k1 k2)) ((union e (KInter r1 (KCons k2 r2)))))   ; proof: proofs/refine_kinter.smt2
(rule ((= e (KInter (KCons k1 r1) (KCons k2 r2))) (< k2 k1)) ((union e (KInter (KCons k1 r1) r2))))   ; proof: proofs/refine_kinter.smt2
(rule ((= e (KInter (KCons k1 r1) (KCons k2 r2))) (= k1 k2)) ((union e (KCons k1 (KInter r1 r2)))))   ; proof: proofs/refine_kinter.smt2
(rewrite (KGuard (T) ks) ks) (rewrite (KGuard (F) ks) (KNil))   ; definitional (conditional)

; ---- KFilt: keep each candidate key iff its subspace is non-empty (the exactness filter) ----
(rewrite (KFilt (KNil) z) (KNil))   ; proof: proofs/keys_filter_exact.smt2
(rewrite (KFilt (KCons h ks) z) (KConsIf h (IsEmpty (Sub h z)) (KFilt ks z)))   ; proof: proofs/keys_filter_exact.smt2
(rewrite (KConsIf h (T) rest) rest)   ; proof: proofs/keys_filter_exact.smt2
(rewrite (KConsIf h (F) rest) (KCons h rest))   ; proof: proofs/keys_filter_exact.smt2
(rewrite (IsNilK (KNil)) (T))   ; proof: proofs/keys_filter_exact.smt2
(rewrite (IsNilK (KCons h ks)) (F))   ; proof: proofs/keys_filter_exact.smt2

; ================================================================================================
; IsEmpty — local where possible; an HONEST SEARCH (via exact Keys) for ∩ \ · <|
; ================================================================================================
(rewrite (IsEmpty (Empty)) (T))   ; proof: proofs/isempty_finite.smt2 (wf tries; structural = terminating)
(rewrite (IsEmpty (Eps)) (F))   ; proof: proofs/isempty_finite.smt2 (wf tries; structural = terminating)
(rewrite (IsEmpty (Src n)) (EmptyOf n))   ; proof: proofs/isempty_finite.smt2 (wf tries; structural = terminating)
(rewrite (IsEmpty (Wrap1 h z)) (IsEmpty z))   ; proof: proofs/isempty_finite.smt2 (wf tries; structural = terminating)
(rewrite (IsEmpty (Union a b)) (And (IsEmpty a) (IsEmpty b)))   ; proof: proofs/isempty_finite.smt2 (wf tries; structural = terminating)
(rewrite (IsEmpty (Guard b z)) (Or (Not b) (IsEmpty z)))   ; proof: proofs/isempty_finite.smt2 (wf tries; structural = terminating)
; the search: empty ⟺ not a member here and no present child key (Keys is exact, so this is IsNilK)
(rewrite (IsEmpty (Intersection a b))   ; proof: proofs/isempty_finite.smt2 (wf tries; structural = terminating)
         (And (Not (Term (Intersection a b))) (IsNilK (Keys (Intersection a b)))))
(rewrite (IsEmpty (Subtraction a b))   ; proof: proofs/isempty_finite.smt2 (wf tries; structural = terminating)
         (And (Not (Term (Subtraction a b))) (IsNilK (Keys (Subtraction a b)))))
(rewrite (IsEmpty (Composition a b))   ; proof: proofs/isempty_finite.smt2 (wf tries; structural = terminating)
         (And (Not (Term (Composition a b))) (IsNilK (Keys (Composition a b)))))
(rewrite (IsEmpty (Restriction x p))   ; proof: proofs/isempty_finite.smt2 (wf tries; structural = terminating)
         (And (Not (Term (Restriction x p))) (IsNilK (Keys (Restriction x p)))))

; ================================================================================================
; tails / Head / Iter — DEFINED through key enumeration (the previously hand-waved part)
; ================================================================================================
(rewrite (TailsUnion z) (KFoldU (Keys z) z))   ; proof: proofs/keyfolds.smt2 + proofs/threeway_tailsunion_trie.smt2
(rewrite (KFoldU (KNil) z) (Empty))   ; proof: proofs/keyfolds.smt2 + proofs/threeway_tailsunion_trie.smt2
(rewrite (KFoldU (KCons h ks) z) (Union (Sub h z) (KFoldU ks z)))   ; proof: proofs/keyfolds.smt2 + proofs/threeway_tailsunion_trie.smt2
(rewrite (TailsIntersection z) (KFoldI (Keys z) z))     ; exact keys: a spurious ∅ would poison the meet   ; proof: proofs/keyfold_tailsinter.smt2
(rewrite (KFoldI (KNil) z) (Empty))   ; proof: proofs/keyfold_tailsinter.smt2
(rewrite (KFoldI (KCons h (KNil)) z) (Sub h z))   ; proof: proofs/keyfold_tailsinter.smt2
(rewrite (KFoldI (KCons h (KCons j ks)) z) (Intersection (Sub h z) (KFoldI (KCons j ks) z)))   ; proof: proofs/keyfold_tailsinter.smt2
(rewrite (Head z) (HFold (Keys z)))                     ; exact keys: no empty-tailed heads   ; proof: proofs/keyfold_head.smt2 + proofs/impl_head.smt2
(rewrite (HFold (KNil)) (Empty))   ; proof: proofs/keyfold_head.smt2 + proofs/impl_head.smt2
(rewrite (HFold (KCons h ks)) (Union (Wrap1 h (Eps)) (HFold ks)))   ; proof: proofs/keyfold_head.smt2 + proofs/impl_head.smt2
(rewrite (Iter z b) (IFold (Keys z) z b))               ; exact keys: bodies see present heads only   ; proof: proofs/keyfold_iter.smt2
(rewrite (IFold (KNil) z b) (Empty))   ; proof: proofs/keyfold_iter.smt2
(rewrite (IFold (KCons h ks) z b) (Union (App b h (Sub h z)) (IFold ks z b)))   ; proof: proofs/keyfold_iter.smt2
; body applications (defunctionalized; programs add their own constructors + one rule each)
(rewrite (App (ConstBody v) h t) v)                                    ; invariant body   ; definitional (body definitions; programs add their own)
(rewrite (App (JoinBody s) h t) (Wrap1 h (TailsUnion (Restriction s t))))   ; the datalog join   ; proof: proofs/join_spec.smt2 (THE datalog join specification)
(rewrite (App (InvBody) b as) (Iter as (InvBody2 b)))                  ; invert: outer head captured…   ; definitional (body definitions; programs add their own)
(rewrite (App (InvBody2 b) a t) (Wrap1 a (Wrap1 b (Eps))))             ; …and swapped below   ; definitional (body definitions; programs add their own)

; ================================================================================================
; algebraic laws (the implemented smart-constructor short-circuits + ring identities)
; ================================================================================================
(rewrite (Union a a) a)   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2
(rewrite (Intersection a a) a)   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2
(rewrite (Subtraction a a) (Empty))   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2
(rewrite (Restriction x x) x)                            ; ported from formal.egg   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2
(rewrite (Union (Empty) x) x) (rewrite (Union x (Empty)) x)   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2
(rewrite (Intersection (Empty) x) (Empty)) (rewrite (Intersection x (Empty)) (Empty))   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2
(rewrite (Subtraction (Empty) x) (Empty)) (rewrite (Subtraction x (Empty)) x)   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2
(rewrite (Composition (Empty) x) (Empty)) (rewrite (Composition x (Empty)) (Empty))   ; proof: proofs/composition_norm.smt2
(rewrite (Wrap1 h (Empty)) (Empty))   ; proof: proofs/pointwise.smt2
(rewrite (Composition (Eps) x) x) (rewrite (Composition x (Eps)) x)   ; proof: proofs/composition_norm.smt2
(rewrite (Composition (Wrap1 h a) b) (Wrap1 h (Composition a b)))   ; proof: proofs/composition_norm.smt2
(rewrite (Composition (Union a b) c) (Union (Composition a c) (Composition b c)))   ; proof: proofs/composition_norm.smt2
; commutativity/associativity of ∪/∩ are NOT syntactic rewrites here (e-graph blow-up; the
; implementation is order-free IntMaps) — they are certified universally in proofs/*.smt2 and
; spot-checked observationally below.

; ================================================================================================
